 "question": "r2130 found the within-quarter cross-book spread of the cadence delta jump in 2025H2 and could not say whether that was a short window, a wide market, or real phase risk from the rule",
 "rule": {
  "R1_same_books": "same six start dates, same cadences 10/20, same n_hold=5, same 8bp cost and same next-open fill as r2130 -- only the segment list is extended",
  "R2_bars_measured": "the bar count of every quarter slice is printed from the same slice call that produced the return; channel A is judged on the measured numbers, not on a belief about short windows",
  "R3_breadth": "breadth = interquartile range of single-name quarterly returns over every column of the tradable panel that has both endpoints finite; this is a property of the market, not of any book",
  "R4_overlap": "for each book, the union of names picked at its rebalance bars inside the quarter (top n_hold by that bar's score, the same rule fast_next_open applies); overlap = mean pairwise Jaccard across the books live in that quarter",
  "R5_null": "4 permutation-score families (per-bar shuffle of the finite entries, seed 20261126). Each null family gets the same per-quarter cross-book spread treatment; the widening is called chance when the actual spread does not clear the largest null",
  "R6_words": "every verdict word is computed from this face's own printed numbers; check recomputes them and fails on any disagreement",
  "R7_thin": "a quarter needs >= 2 live books to have a cross-book spread at all; thin cells and partial quarters are named, never zeroed",
  "R8_money": "money lines use a 1000000 reference account and quarter total returns, not annualised"
 },
